-------------------------------------------------------------------------
A. Introduction
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

This example shows how to implement a basic functioning UVM testbench using I2C
Verification IP. A quickstart navigation guide can be found at:
    
HTML Quickstart is available @ $DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/i2c_svt/latest/examples/sverilog/tb_i2c_svt_uvm_basic_sys/doc/i2c_uvm_basic/index_basic.html
    
The example consists of the following:

- A top-level testbench in SystemVerilog
- A hdl_interconnect representing the I2C bus in the testbench and master I2C 
  and Slave I2C interfaces are connected to hdl_interconnect
- UVM verification environment
- I2C master and I2C slave agents are instantiated in the UVM verification environment
- Three test files illustrating 
  i.   Basic test with default sequence
  ii.  Directed test with directed sequences
  iii. Random test with random sequence

The UVM Synopsys Discovery I2C VIP agents are connected in the following manner:

                                     (I2C Env)
    ==================================================================================
  ||     (I2C Master Agent)                                      (I2C Slave Agent)    ||
  ||   ---------------------                                    -------------------   ||
  ||  |  ------    -------  |                                  |  -----   -------  |  ||
  ||  | |Master|  |Monitor| |        ------------------        | |Slave| |Monitor| |  ||
  ||  |  ------    -------  |<=====>| hdl_interconnect |<=====>|  -----   -------  |  ||
  ||  |    *Active Mode*    |        ------------------        |   *Active Mode*   |  ||
  ||   \___________________/                                    \_________________/   ||
  ||                                                                                  ||
    ==================================================================================


In the remainder of this description, <design_dir> refers to the directory where
the example was installed using script dw_vip_setup. The example source files
would then exist at two locations:

- "$DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/i2c_svt/latest/examples/sverilog/tb_i2c_svt_uvm_basic_sys" 
- "<design_dir>/examples/sverilog/i2c_svt/tb_i2c_svt_uvm_basic_sys" 

Note :- the quickstart guide is _only_ available at
$DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/i2c_svt/latest/examples/sverilog/tb_i2c_svt_uvm_basic_sys/doc/tb_i2c_svt_uvm_basic_sys/index_basic.html

The quickstart is not installed in <design_dir>. Unless otherwise noted, the files
described below are also found in <design_dir>.  

Complete class reference HTML documentation of I2C UVM Verification 
IP is available at:
  
$DESIGNWARE_HOME/vip/svt/i2c_svt/latest/doc/i2c_svt_uvm_class_reference/html/index.html
------------------------------------------------------------------------
B. Running the Example Testbench
------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Install the example using the following command line:

   % cd <location where example is to be installed>
   % mkdir design_dir <provide any name of your choice>
   % $DESIGNWARE_HOME/bin/dw_vip_setup -path ./design_dir  -e i2c_svt/tb_i2c_svt_uvm_basic_sys -svtb 

2. Use either one of the following to run the testbench:

   a) Use the Makefile:

      Three tests are provided in the "tests" directory.
      The tests are: 
      1. ts.base_test.sv 
      2. ts.directed_test.sv 
      3. ts.random_test.sv 

      For example, to run test ts.directed_test.sv, do following:
      
      gmake USE_SIMULATOR=vcsvlog directed_test WAVES=1

      Invoke "gmake help" to show more options.
   
   b) Use the sim script:

    1) For example, to run test ts.random_test.sv on VCS simulator, do following:

     ./run_i2c_svt_uvm_basic_sys -w random_test vcsvlog-svlog 

    2) For example, to run test ts.random_test.sv on NC simulator, do following:

     ./run_i2c_svt_uvm_basic_sys random_test ncvlog-svlog 

      Invoke "./run_i2c_svt_uvm_basic_sys -help" to show more options.


