-------------------------------------------------------------------------
D. SystemVerilog Testbench Description
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The  top-level testbench is written in SystemVerilog. The I2C interfaces 
are represented as instances of 'interface' objects. The hdl_interconnect 
is represented as a I2C bus model with 'interface' connections as its ports.
The UVM verification environment is represented as an i2c_basic_env instance.
The test file is created as a class which extends i2c_base_test.

The file containing the top-level testbench in the example is "top.sv".  
This file which encapsulates individual tests is "top_test.sv".

The I2C bus model used in the example is defined as a hdl_interconnect, within a SystemVerilog
wrapper. The intent is to demonstrate how a legacy core may be integrated into
the SystemVerilog testbench. The example I2C bus model has master and slave I2C interfaces. 


The SystemVerilog wrapper for the I2C bus model defines a module that takes 'interface'
references as its port connections. The SystemVerilog wrapper instantiates
the Verilog I2C bus model, and connects I2C master and slave interfaces to the I2C bus model.

The example I2C bus model is found in the file "hdl_interconnect.v". The example wrapper
is found in the file "i2c_svt_interconnect_sv_wrapper.sv".

The entire UVM test environment is encapsulated in i2c_basic_env.sv, which is
instantiated in the UVM tests.  The tests gets included in 'top.sv',
which eventually triggers the specific test by the use of run_test().
  

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
E. UVM Verification Environment Description
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

A complete description of the UVM environment (ENV) is beyond the scope of this
README. Please refer to the UVM manual for details of a UVM environment.

Following is a summary of the files used by the ENV:

  - i2c_svt_interconnect_sv_wrapper.sv.  A SystemVerilog module that wraps the
    verilog RTL Interconnect.  This will be instantiated in the top-level SystemVerilog
    file.
  
  - i2c_basic_env.sv
    This file serves as environment class.  The top-level environment is
    implemented by extending uvm_env base class.  This class instantiates the
    I2C Master agent, I2C Slave agent and a virtual sequencer.

  - cust_svt_i2c_configuration.sv
    This file has a class cust_svt_i2c_agent_configuration that extends from svt_i2c_agent_configuration.
    All the necessary configuration parameters are set up for the environment 
    in this class.

  - cust_svt_i2c_master_transaction.sv
    This file extends the master transaction (svt_i2c_master_transaction).
    Customized constraints are defined by this class.

 -  cust_svt_i2c_slave_transaction.sv
    This file extends the slave transaction (svt_i2c_slave_transaction).
    Customized constraints are defined by this class.

  - i2c_simple_reset_sequence.sv
    This file shows a sequence that generates a reset sequence
    to drive the reset pins.  This sequence is registered with the TB
    virtual sequencer as the default sequence for the reset phase.

  - i2c_default_virtual_sequence.sv
    This file implements a virtual sequence and executes master and slave sequences.
    This sequence is registered with the I2C System ENV virtual sequencer as 
    the default sequence for the main phase.

  - i2c_null_virtual_sequence.sv
    This file implements a virtual sequence with an empty body method.  This
    sequence can be used by extended tests to disable the default sequence.

  - i2c_mst_random_sequence.sv
    This file shows a master sequence (extending from uvm_sequence)
    that generates constrained random svt_i2c_master_transaction.  

  - i2c_slv_random_sequence.sv
    This file shows a slave sequence (extending from uvm_sequence)
    that generates constrained random svt_i2c_slave_transaction.

  - i2c_mst_directed_sequence.sv
    This file shows a master sequence (extending from uvm_sequence)
    that generates a series of directed svt_i2c_master_transaction.

  - i2c_slv_directed_sequence.sv
    This file shows a slave sequence (extending from uvm_sequence)
    that generates a series of directed svt_i2c_slave_transaction.

  - i2c_default_mst_sequence.sv
    This file shows a master sequence (extending from uvm_sequence)
    that generates a default random svt_i2c_master_transaction.

  - i2c_default_slv_sequence.sv
    This file shows a slave sequence (extending from uvm_sequence)
    that generates a default random svt_i2c_slave_transaction.

